Hi:

Look at the examples in ?plyr::ozone - they mirror the previous advice
you were given. It's likely that plyr had changed sufficiently since
the paper was published to make this example throw an error.

The problem is that the output of rlm() is a list, which you can
observe by looking at the preceding code block in the paper that you
omitted:

one <- ozone[1, 1, ]
month <- ordered(rep(1:12, length = 72))
model <- rlm(one ~ month - 1)
str(model)

so you really should be using alply() to get a list of models before
extracting the residuals. Alternatively, you could rewrite the
function to extract the residuals from the fitted model object and
return them directly since resid() is an extraction function. This
works for me with the current version of plyr:

deseasf <- function(value) resid(rlm(value ~ month - 1))
deseas <- aaply(ozone, 1:2, deseasf)

Dennis

