Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/i0Re22tkV8U/m/CmQfHW34hbQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

My question is about how to structure/ tidy/ organize data.

Given a df users:

Users <- data.frame(Name = c("Alice", "Bob", "Cathy"), City = c("New York", "Dallas", "Los Angeles"))

In reality Users has many observations.

The Problem: I would like to add a 'route' for each user to get to, say, Chicago.  The route will be a series of lat/long, but will be of non-standard length: everyone's route will be different in number of steps.

I am using ggmap to do this, where

library(ggmap)
route(from = 'New York', to = 'Chicago', structure = 'route')

returns a data frame.

How should I properly store this data frame for each User observation?

From u373beb702917b8b5 at groups.google.com  Wed Dec 31 02:19:37 2014
From: u373beb702917b8b5 at groups.google.com (Ista Zahn)
Date: Wed, 31 Dec 2014 02:19:37 +0000
Subject: Re: How to Structure Varying Length Vector/DF Data
Message-ID: <i0Re22tkV8U.PsLM0MAow2gJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <i0Re22tkV8U.CmQfHW34hbQJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
References: <i0Re22tkV8U.CmQfHW34hbQJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/i0Re22tkV8U/m/PsLM0MAow2gJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Well, the dplyr way is just to put the data frames inside the dataframe:

Users %>%
  group_by(Name, City) %>%
  do(
  route = route(from = as.character(.$City),

                to = 'Chicago',
                structure = 'route')

  ) -> UserRoutes

I used to be very skeptical of this approach, but I've come around.

Best,
Ista

